{
  "metric": "FixRate-WorsenRate",
  "definition_id": "offline_policy_matched_terminal_counterfactual",
  "definition": "Hold-out weak steps plus the saved closed-loop policy. A scored pair is a teacher step in {CORRECT_CODE, RE_PORTION, RE_DECOMPOSE} whose policy prediction equals that action, on a dish that ends at STOP with a finite nutri_dish energy (pass or corrected). Before/after dish energy is that STOP total with the corrected component swapped to its pre-correction energy. RE_PORTION uses the obs portion ratio. CORRECT_CODE swaps the old code's component energy for the new code at the same pre-portion grams, so a later RE_PORTION on that component is not credited to the code change. Error is absolute kcal versus the train-split cafe dish label. Fix: error falls by more than epsilon. Worsen: error rises by more than epsilon. Otherwise neutral. Rates share the scored-pair denominator. Scope: offline logged tool results and the saved policy checkpoint.",
  "epsilon_kcal": 1.0,
  "epsilon_rule": "fix if (err_before - err_after) > epsilon; worsen if (err_after - err_before) > epsilon; otherwise neutral",
  "error": "absolute dish energy kcal versus the train-split cafe label",
  "budget_K": 32,
  "budget_K_source": "vdr.controller.features.STEP_BUDGET and vdr.controller.state_features.TOOL_CAP",
  "ci_method": "Percentile cluster bootstrap over dishes. Each draw resamples dishes with replacement and keeps every scored pair from those dishes. B=10000, seed=0, quantiles 2.5 and 97.5. Each rate block restarts the generator at the same seed. Wilson intervals are not used: fix and worsen are mutually exclusive outcomes of the same pairs, so the contrast is a paired trinomial mean.",
